const HELP_NEWS = "## 1.162.7 - 2026-11-14\n\n- Phone and PC: asking for an area's folder again is shorter, and says\n  1 of 2, then 2 of 2, when more than one area waits (#346). The browser\n  asks for one folder per click, so each area asks on its own. The panel\n  and the dialog now say the same thing.\n\n## 1.162.6 - 2026-11-14\n\n- Phone and PC: after Allow access, the folder's pages take over when you\n  press Enter at the end of a line (#181). They waited until you left the\n  line, so capturing line after line kept the folder out. The page you\n  write in comes along as it is, with the caret on the new line, and is\n  merged with its file when saved.\n\n## 1.162.5 - 2026-11-14\n\n- Vault and sync: Save log (#181) now starts with what holds today's page\n  back. For each area: when today's page was on screen and from where\n  (the folder or the browser copy), when Allow access was tapped, what the\n  switch to the folder waited for (a line being typed, saves, the merge),\n  and when the folder was listed and read, each with its time. Then the\n  slowest folders to list, a file read on its own against 16 at a time,\n  and how many files were unchanged since the last read. Every step\n  follows, as before.\n\n## 1.162.4 - 2026-11-14\n\n- Vault and sync: after Allow access on a phone, today's page from the\n  folder shows within seconds (#181). The copy from browser storage gave\n  way only once the whole folder was listed, half a minute or more, and a\n  new day could not start until then. Now the folder takes over as soon as\n  today's page is in; the rest is listed and read behind it.\n\n## 1.162.3 - 2026-11-14\n\n- Vault and sync: today's page shows in seconds on a big folder (#181).\n  It is opened by its name before the folder is listed, and you can write\n  in it at once. Yesterday's page follows, for what was written before\n  midnight. Only then is the rest of the folder listed and read, as before.\n  A page made in those first seconds is saved once the folder is listed.\n\n## 1.162.2 - 2026-11-14\n\n- Journal: a phone opens on the Journal, as a wider screen does, not on\n  Next. A phone is mostly for capture; Next is one tap away.\n\n## 1.162.1 - 2026-11-14\n\n- Keys on a line: the test for brackets that come in pairs (#268) puts the\n  caret in the line first, as typing does. It failed every time before,\n  though brackets worked.\n\n## 1.162.0 - 2026-11-14\n\n- Keys on a line: a phone has no Shift key, so the bar at the foot of the\n  screen while you write now has Notepad (#392). It opens the notepad at\n  the caret, as Shift+Enter does.\n\n## 1.161.1 - 2026-11-14\n\n- Keys on a line: after lines are picked by dragging the mouse, the next\n  click is no longer lost when the button was let go outside the window\n  (#392). The click on a dialog's button, such as the notepad's Replace\n  all, did nothing.\n\n## 1.161.0 - 2026-11-14\n\n- People › List: contacts to and from the phone, as vCard (.vcf) files\n  (#383). On a person's page, ⋯ › Share contact hands them to the phone's\n  share sheet, which offers Add contact, or saves the file. Export people\n  saves everyone in the area as one file. Import contacts reads a .vcf and\n  shows each person as New, Changed or Same; nothing is written before\n  Import. Chrome on Android can also pick straight from the phone's\n  contacts. Name, phone, email, organisation and birthday map to phone::,\n  email::, org:: and birthday::.\n\n## 1.160.0 - 2026-11-14\n\n- Keys on a line: Shift+Enter opens the notepad (#392). It shows the line\n  and the lines under it in a fixed-width box, with the caret's line and\n  column, and Find and Replace. A sketch drawn there keeps its lines and\n  spaces; the file keeps it in a code fence. Done or Ctrl+Enter saves.\n  Shift+Enter no longer adds a line under the line; Enter after ``` still\n  does.\n\n## 1.159.0 - 2026-11-14\n\n- Weekly review › Steps: a #meeting on a coming day page that links an\n  active project, on its own line or a line above it, keeps the project\n  off Stuck active projects (#385). Cancelled meetings and meetings that\n  only name people do not count. Once the day has passed with no new to do\n  or waiting for, the project is stuck again with \"Meeting held - process\n  the notes\".\n";
